new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/eval/graders/multiple_runtime/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# MultiPL-E runtime
+
+Build the two images from the Evalchemy checkout:
+
+```sh
+docker build --platform linux/amd64 -t verifyit-evalchemy-multiple:source-v1 -f eval/graders/multiple_runtime/Dockerfile .
+docker build --platform linux/arm64 -t verifyit-evalchemy-multiple-native:source-v1 -f eval/graders/multiple_runtime/Dockerfile.csharp .
+```
+
+The first image derives from the immutable image named by the source README.
+It repairs the image's Swift and Julia PATH entries and installs the pinned Ada
+and Racket packages that the corresponding source callbacks require. The native
+ARM64 image supplies Mono and Racket because those runtimes abort under AMD64
+emulation on the validation host. Source and cutover comparisons use the same
+image and architecture for each language. This is an explicit runtime change,
+not evidence that the original AMD64 image works on every host.
+
+The opt-in adapter chooses the native image for C# and Racket and the source-derived
+image for other supported languages. VERIFYIT_MULTIPLE_IMAGE and
+VERIFYIT_MULTIPLE_PLATFORM override that trusted execution configuration together
+when an installation supplies an equivalent runtime. Neither value comes from a
+candidate response. Images must be built before grading; missing Docker or tools
+abort the batch with an infrastructure failure rather than a candidate score.
+
+All 31 advertised source selectors remain in the integration census. Twenty-four
+have bundled task data and source scoring modules. Ruby, D, and OCaml use their
+actual bundled rb/d/ml filenames; Ada, Perl, and Scala receive their existing
+source callback dispatch. Seven selectors lack bundled populations and are
+rejected explicitly. Source generation also lacks formatting settings for some
+advertised selectors; this adapter does not claim to repair that separate driver.
+
+The trusted source test program and candidate run together in the retained
+runtime, preserving source language semantics. This is a candidate-in-grader
+bridge, not isolation of trusted assertions from candidate execution. The parent
+owns a named container and removes it on success, failure, or timeout. Source
+per-language subprocess deadlines remain in force inside the configured sample
+deadline, with 40 seconds allowed for container setup and shutdown.
+
+Two scoring corrections are deliberate. Go test programs use `_test.go` so the
+Go tool actually discovers Test functions. All callbacks must report both status
+`OK` and exit code zero: the source outer scorer checks only exit code, which can
+credit Mono or other runtimes after their callback reports failed assertions.
+Unsuccessful source statuses remain candidate zero; missing executable or import
+errors abort the batch. Source pass@k estimation and selected-task denominator
+remain unchanged. The adapter regenerates scores from current responses and does
+not accept stale generated response files.
